1002 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H4
/P 492 0 R
/T (For small loops, the compiler already performs full unrolling automatically, so adding #pragma unroll\(4\) can degrade performance by reintroducing loop control instructions. However, for large loops, full unrolling is not feasible. In this case, #pragma unroll\(4\) enables partial unrolling, reducing loop overhead and increasing instruction-level parallelism.)
/E (For small loops, the compiler already performs full unrolling automatically, so adding #pragma unroll\(4\) can degrade performance by reintroducing loop control instructions. However, for large loops, full unrolling is not feasible. In this case, #pragma unroll\(4\) enables partial unrolling, reducing loop overhead and increasing instruction-level parallelism.)
/Pg 36 0 R
/K [21]
>>
